linger: off. systemd stops slop-bot when your last session ends; to keep it running with nobody logged in (a headless box), run: loginctl enable-linger

If these don't suit:
  - to move a location, export its XDG_* variable in your shell profile and re-run `slop-bot install`:
    the service takes its paths from the shell that installs it (all but XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, which systemd sets)
  - edit the config (repos, harnesses, workspace_dir) and the briefing, then run `slop-bot doctor`;
    re-running `slop-bot install` keeps both and restarts the service
  - `slop-bot uninstall` removes the service; add --purge to delete slop-bot's data too

